        "header": "3Method",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.25690/2610.25690v1/method_pipeline.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Overview of ScaleNav. (a) Language-conditioned local navigation.The model predicts video and action chunks from the instruction, current observation, and memory using chunk-wise causal attention. The memory contains an initial-frame anchor and a sliding window of recent video and action chunks.(b) Three-stage training.Video pretraining uses action-free real videos, followed by action alignment and joint fine-tuning with action-labeled simulation data. During action alignment, the self-attention layers within the DiT, the action head, and the action embedding MLP (not shown) are trainable. The snowflake on the outer DiT block marks the remaining DiT layers as frozen. Joint fine-tuning updates the DiT and both heads. For clarity, the initial bidirectional adaptation in Stage 1 and Internet egocentric video replay in Stages 2 and 3 are omitted.",
                "position": 450
            }
        ]
    },
